Define the question and audience of a scientific report (@inquiry-report-question: 0, is #chapter, #hephaestus-core "Connect-each-claim-to-observations-methods-and-premises.lingua#r_00085ECCDE383B7726ECB440F6") { r_00B75D987D4D8ED671FEFD6861
A scientific report lets another person understand a claim, reconstruct its support and challenge its limits. Begin with the question, useful quantity and evidence, before choosing headings or drawing a figure. Reuse [Make an argument understandable challengeable and preservable](Make-an-argument-understandable-challengeable-and-preservable.lingua#r_094622380644F206A98B67A516) and [Review fitting evidence before extending scientific claims](Review fitting evidence before extending scientific claims.lingua#r_008E6FD7D2B90DB8ED1CE9927E). An accurate calculation can support an inaccurate sentence when its conditions disappear between the notebook and the conclusion.

The running question is deliberately small: how do a shared offset, curvature and a corrected input affect an affine fit and what can its residuals establish? Use the existing [Investigate fitting uncertainty and competing observation models](Investigate fitting uncertainty and competing observation models.lingua#r_00FEC32E133E78D019BFE134C2) unchanged. The input levels x=(−2,−1,0,1,2) and constructed responses y=2+3x+e, e=(1,−1,1,−1,1), are dimensionless teaching values. They are not measurements. The exact fitted intercept is 11/5, slope 3 and residual sum of squares 24/5. The generating intercept 2 and fitted intercept 11/5 have different meanings even in this fully known construction.

The intended reader knows arithmetic and has reached the earlier fitting argument. A short report must explain what was compared, how the numbers were made and what remains unknown. An extended evidence package adds the original rows, method files, environment, exact outputs and revision record. Neither reader should have to guess whether a number is a physical observation, a model input, an estimate, a standard deviation or a stipulated bound.

State the population or domain the claim addresses. Here it is four explicitly constructed finite datasets and an unweighted affine fitting method. Fixed input levels, paired response values, equal weights and retained observations define the calculation. Zero-mean, uncorrelated, equal-variance errors are additional premises for interpreting SSE/(n−2) as an estimator of common observation variance. The deterministic rows alone do not demonstrate those premises. No probability distribution, confidence level, instrument accuracy or general physical law follows from the exact arithmetic.

An original bounded claim is: the supplied offset case shifts the fitted intercept by 2 and preserves slope and residuals; therefore residual agreement alone cannot detect that shared response offset. This follows by substitution and is checked by the existing program. An independently referenced response observation could distinguish the physical alternatives if its own uncertainty and reference conditions were known. That observation is proposed, not performed.

**Beginner work:** explain the claim in five sentences without statistical terminology, then add the precise mathematical version. Predict what a constant response shift does before computing it. Give a counterexample to the statement that small residuals prove accurate calibration. Transfer the question to the bias/disturbance ambiguity in [Separate disturbance rejection from sensor bias and identifiable quantities](../../engineering/core/Separate-disturbance-rejection-from-sensor-bias-and-identifiable-quantities.lingua#r_0089FCA742A41805791FE10944) and identify what additional evidence each setting needs.

**Reading:** use [Good enough practices in scientific computing — Wilson and colleagues](../reproducible-computation/sources/Scientific-Computing-Practices.lingua#r_5J8HXCQDNJH59EZC1PRJTQK38B) for organizing a report that others can enter and challenge. The inspected manuscript and collaboration passages support this practice; the present datasets, numerical report and teaching argument are original.

**Continue:** [Connect each claim to observations methods and premises](Connect-each-claim-to-observations-methods-and-premises.lingua#r_00085ECCDE383B7726ECB440F6).

